From b30e0d08bf1cdb8a6c6d6a7c24d4fee8f2148ba3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:53:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] CUDA/HIP: fused relative-position bias for one token;
 memory safety for the single-token fusions

- new fusion MUL_MAT(r, table) -> SUB(sinks) -> GET_ROWS(distance) -> CONT ->
  ADD(mask) -> CPY(F16): one kernel computes only the gathered entries,
  (<r_h, table_rel[i]> - sinks[h]) + mask[i] in F16, instead of the whole
  [n_head, n_extent + 1] table and four more kernels (Inkling 2, per layer)
- fix: the fused single-token kernels (conv step, depth mix, controller mix,
  MUL + L2_NORM, relative bias) run at the first node of their pattern but
  write the output of the last, which the allocator may place over an input
  that dies inside the pattern. They now fuse only when no output overlaps an
  input read across threads (element-wise inputs may be the output itself),
  and graph_optimize adds alloc deps for them so that this stays the common
  case. Before, a batch-1 perplexity run over several chunks went NaN once the
  allocator reused Rcur's memory for the bias.

R9700 Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL tg128 51.0 -> 54.0 tok/s, 2337 -> 2138
kernels per token; KLD vs the original build at batch 1 over 4 chunks 0.0018.
New test-backend-ops case REL_BIAS.
